            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-09-01T20:55:31.896309+00:00",
            "notes": "My cute final build.... I'll end up getting  [Weapon Jammer](item_72386db6-753e-413d-aa2a-f1389842f47f) to increase my own attack speed and to debuff the enemies. I'll also go with  [El-sa'ka Supressor](item_b4298dd9-9b93-461f-a2e0-843402667100) to debuff them even more if I have the cash. If I do not have enough cash, I'll opt to buy back  [Advanced Nanobiotics](item_26fcf7c9-b81a-4d8e-a459-b515519cb73e) and  [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) to makeup for the lack of debuffs.\n\nFor the power, I usually end up doing a flex depending on what my team needs this last round. If I'm finding it difficult to survive I go with  [Serenity](item_c6e1c072-ff50-467e-b59f-9506baea10c1) so I can be healed passively. This is especially good if you choose  [Threads of Fate](item_cb61612b-9d83-49a9-989d-013bf084fbcb) the first round, as you now are healed constantly. If my teammates are doing great and I want to enable them more, I'll go with  [Distortion](item_5557e2f2-02df-4eac-8128-0c23b71183b1) for the lifesteal my teammates get. However, if I find that I'm still not providing enough healing, I'll go with  [Triage Unit](item_fec0554c-2685-4b93-822d-bf0020e654b4), which allows me to heal my teammates who are under half health much easier. This perk pairs well with  [Amari's Antidote](item_67e0b1c5-3bcb-4ab5-b818-5082e5706124) so it's nice to use.",
